    "text": "96\n\n What You Need to Know About Accounting Practice Deals - From the Trenches!\nHi Sara,\nThe accounting industry is evolving at lightning speed, that\u2019s not a surprise to anyone who has a pulse.\u00a0\nPrivate equity, valuation inflation, rising interest rates\u2014these trends are reshaping the way accounting firms are built, run, and bought.\nI recently was honored to be invited to join Marcus Dillon, CPA, and Rachel Dillon on their podcast Who\u2019s Really the Boss? to unpack the biggest shifts happening in accounting firm ownership.\u00a0\nIf you\u2019re in the industry\u2014or just curious about how these changes could ripple into other businesses\u2014you\u2019ll want to tune in.\nHere are some highlights from our conversation:\nPhantom Equity Plans Are Everywhere\nTraditional partnerships? Not always the answer. Phantom equity plans are gaining ground, allowing firms to align team incentives without handing over direct ownership. It\u2019s a win-win for firms and employees alike.\nRemote Teams, Real Compliance Challenges\nRemote work is the new normal, but compliance hasn\u2019t caught up. From payroll laws to data security, accounting firm owners are navigating murky waters. We break down the common pitfalls and how to avoid them.\nNew Buyers Are Entering the Game and Changing the Rules\nIt\u2019s not just CPAs buying firms anymore. Private equity and other non-traditional buyers are changing the playing field, and they\u2019re bringing big opportunities\u2014and challenges\u2014with them.\nMillennial Owners Are Shifting Priorities\u00a0\nYounger owners are rethinking what success looks like. Work-life balance, profitability, and sustainable growth are at the forefront, and it\u2019s influencing how deals are structured.\nThe big takeaway? The accounting industry is no longer \u201cbusiness as usual.\u201d Owners, buyers, and teams are rewriting the rules.\n\ud83c\udfa7 [Listen to the episode here]\nAs someone who works in the trenches of mergers, acquisitions, and compliance, I love seeing how these shifts are creating opportunities for firms to grow, innovate, and thrive.\nWhat am I missing? I\u2019d love to hear your thoughts\u2014just hit reply!\nHere\u2019s to staying ahead of the curve,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nBusiness Consultant and Founder of Deal Academy\n--\nFor more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers podcast episodes by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
